Boudewijn Waijers wrote:

> Does anyone know how I can get NetHack to display the high score list?

Sorry to reply to my own posting, but I figured it out myself.

My nhs.bat file contains:

  nethack -s -v all
  pause

And it is called by a link on the desktop which reads:

  "C:\Program Files\Games\NetHack\343\NHS.bat"

and has 80x300 buffer size and 80x40 window size. The latter (40) is
necessary to make windows display a scroll bar to the right. Since there
are at most 100 scores in the list, 300 lines should normally be more
than enough.

(Just in case there are more hackers that are interested in displaying
the high score list...)

